    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d849">

                <pb facs="0843" n="677" xml:id="pg677"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 711.5914/143</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister Egan </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-09-15T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 15, 1916, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>167. Your 342, September 14. While I appreciate the courtesy of Foreign Minister
                    in promptly agreeing to an exchange of notes in regard to church property, I
                    would prefer that the exchange of notes be made here between Mr. Brun and
                    myself, as we were the Plenipotentiaries of our respective Governments in the
                    negotiation and signing of the treaty. I trust the Foreign Minister will
                    telegraph to Mr. Brun the Danish text of the note which you telegraphed me, as I
                    cannot use your translation because it was transmitted to the Department in the
                    confidential green cipher.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
